  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "The number of molecules or ions from the following, which do not have odd number of electrons are _____ .<br />(A) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math><br />(B) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>ICl</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup></math><br />(C) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BrF</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math><br />(D) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>ClO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math><br />(E) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></msubsup></math><br />(F) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NO</mi></math>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>ICl</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>BrF</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></msubsup></math>&nbsp;do not have odd number of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;as we can see from their lewis structures respectively:<br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/77dbd89c-82ae-4d8b-a1bb-31c7044d459e-11.PNG\" style=\"width: 160px; height: 134px;\" />,&nbsp;<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/1c1f3f3a-837c-4a83-b2e1-5eaf9009aa72-12.PNG\" style=\"width: 160px; height: 96px;\" />&nbsp;and<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/5becd639-b7d1-4b8c-beba-f33101108629-13.PNG\" style=\"width: 160px; height: 52px;\" /></p><p>The number of electrons in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mrow><mn>23</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NO</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>15</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>ClO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mrow><mn>33</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;are odd.</p>",
